    <div class="about-text reveal d1">
      <span class="eyebrow">Fencing &amp; gates</span>
      <h2>A fence is only as strong <span class="text-highlight">as its posts.</span></h2>
        <p>Most fences that fail don't fail at the panels — they fail at the posts. Posts need to be set deep and firm enough to take the load when the wind catches a run of fencing, and that matters even more in exposed gardens near the coast.</p>
        <p>We'll talk you through the options for your boundary — timber or concrete posts, gravel boards, standard panels, close-board or decorative screening — and recommend what suits your garden, your budget and how long you want it to last.</p>
        <h3>Gates</h3>
        <p>From a wide five-bar timber gate across a driveway to a side gate by the house, we hang gates to swing and close properly, and make sure the posts either side are up to the job.</p>
        <p>Fencing often goes hand in hand with other work, so if you're also planning a <a href="patios.html">patio</a>, <a href="driveways.html">driveway</a> or new lawn, we can price it all together.</p>
